60836619406516,"n":2155}},"short":{"bands":[{"lo":0,"hi":50,"n":33804,"R":-0.06514330333469165,"ret":-0.0019871869926466963,"win":0.34815406460773873},{"lo":50,"hi":70,"n":36574,"R":-0.021458614233355846,"ret":-0.0003129710966984654,"win":0.35968174112757695},{"lo":70,"hi":80,"n":18675,"R":-0.048808363194824574,"ret":-0.0008529519397851635,"win":0.3511111111111111},{"lo":80,"hi":90,"n":9950,"R":-0.06471104560678424,"ret":-0.0015296008167655633,"win":0.342713567839196},{"lo":90,"hi":101,"n":4604,"R":-0.10067073680108153,"ret":-0.0019891123377745318,"win":0.3392701998262381}],"base":{"R":-0.04831517891242585,"ret":-0.0011478737227745028},"top5":{"R":-0.045118987624203986,"ret":-0.000574138128282129,"R_all":-0.060172937830062063,"ret_all":-0.0013809098457122021,"n":2155}}},"extras":[{"side":"long","check":"Open interest up 5%+ in 7 days while the price rose","yes":0.09,"n_yes":2047,"no":0.393,"n_no":4165},{"side":"long","check":"Longs were 60%+ of liquidations over 3 days","yes":0.367,"n_yes":4305,"no":0.166,"n_no":2118},{"side":"long","check":"24h volume at most 10% of the market cap","yes":0.027,"n_yes":9829,"no":-0.184,"n_no":6277},{"side":"long","check":"Circulating supply up 2%+ in 30 days","yes":-0.127,"n_yes":2118,"no":0.03,"n_no":12329},{"side":"short","check":"Circulating supply up 2%+ in 30 days","yes":0.104,"n_yes":2147,"no":0.016,"n_no":12449},{"side":"short","check":"Funding above 0.01% per 8 hours","yes":-0.049,"n_yes":1795,"no":0.184,"n_no":15920}],"findings":["Buying a coin near its 90-day low works when its momentum has come back and its volatility is squeezed (the 'coiled bottom'). Longs scoring 90+ made +4.4% per trade on average after fees, 55% winners, and were positive in 2024, 2026.","Buying a coin only because it is near its low did not work: those trades lost money on average. The turn has to show first (daily RSI back above 45, a squeeze, a higher low).","For 90+ longs the chance of a +50% move within 30 days stayed about the same as for any coin (15% vs 15%) while the chance of a 30% fall was 16% instead of 29%: the upside stays open, the downside shrinks.","Shorting coins that bounce inside a downtrend, away from their lows, made money every year: shorts scoring 90+ made +5.1% per trade. Shorting coins that sit on their lows did not.","The 2x to 3x months you named mostly started while the coin was still falling with weak momentum: WLD in May 2026 and NIL in April 2026 never scored above 65 in the month before. NIL did score 80 on 26 July 2026, days before its August run, but the tested exit took +3% and was out before the big move. No rule we tested could pick these in advance, because the same picture more often kept falling. The score aims for many good trades with small losses instead of one lucky one.","Smart money and fundamentals, where history exists: longs did worse when leverage piled in during the rise (open interest up 5%+ in a week: +0.09R per trade vs +0.39R) and when unlocks added 2%+ supply in a month (-0.13R vs +0.03R); the same unlocks helped shorts (+0.10R vs +0.02R), and shorts did worse when funding was high (-0.05R vs +0.18R). These checks move the score by a few points; the Hyperliquid top traders have no history to test and only nudge it.","Day trades on hourly candles lost money after fees with every selection we tried, and on 4-hour candles they were close to zero. The edge is in holding swing trades for days to weeks.","Realistic growth: about 1.2x to 1.7x a year at 2% to 3% risk per trade, with drops of 20% to 35% along the way. $500 to $1M in two years would need about 2,000x; nothing tested comes close, and a bigger size mostly raises the chance of losing the account."]}